<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>That chilled Sarah; she had heard the rumours. First the tank regiments, then a police force. Apparently, the Ghetto was seceding from Ulyssia. The were checkpoints at all the tourists roads in. Passports were being stamped or, in the absence of passports, flyers for fried chicken joints were stamped; a tourist was expected to sticky-tape the official Memphis-style document into their passports before their next visit. There was a rumour a government was being set up, and a house of parliament had been selected.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91It used to be a strip joint,\'92 the chief rumour monger\'97one Kathy Logan\'97had said at the time.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah stood at the window. She didn\'92t need to peel back the lace curtains to know what was out there. Still, she closed her eyes to block it out, to block everything out. The grounds of the mansion were packed with Elvi pilgrims\'97some camping in tents; others ensconced in creaky motor homes, or sleeping in back of their battered-up Lincoln Mark IVs, while day trippers sat on beach towels and picnicked on porcine small-goods and drank calorie-laden cocktails. Hanging off every utterance Tony made, they breathlessly waited for the next lyric rewrite which united the Elvi in ever deeper unanimous spiritual bliss. Enraptured, they believed the day would come, when the Elvi would cease the senseless lyric-fuelled violence that possessed them in nightclubs and karaoke bars. It would stop once and for all. Now, the Great Teacher walked among them, and gave them beatitudes that soothed the soul. Hence the heretical 
\f1\i Can F*** Me Drain
\f3\i0  (and other more heinous ditties) became 
