\f3\i0 , which the Elvi found intensely soul-elevating, assuming it to be about evolving from their squabbling internecine ways, not realising Tony wrote to it lampoon his onetime friend Alexander Koalemos.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Even as the grounds swelled beyond capacity and the Elvi encampment suppurated beyond the gates and spilled into the neighbourhood, no pilgrim violated the threshold of the house itself, even though they were all clones of one series or another, at least superficially interchangeable, and could easily pass for one of the staff or official entourage.  They were all in awe of the Sanctity of the Holy Momma and the Word of the Great Teacher, and would brook no invasion of their privacy.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah felt her inhibitions slither away as the patch worked its magic. Before she\'92d considered, she grabbed her tablet and hailed. Alexander\'92s puke-worthy mug flickered onto the screen\'97round and fuzzy at the edges, with beady, too-bright eyes, a snub little nose, and ears that seemed to be sprouting their own sideburns. There was something about that face: uncanny, almost koala-cute, but just off enough to make Sarah want to disinfect her screen.\
